summary:
  The number of the last MPRIS command obeyed is kept in a 32-bit int, so every
  line of the command file looks new on every read.

history:
  The bridge numbers its commands with the time in milliseconds (about
  1.79e12) since 2026-09-22, and the widget went on keeping the last one in a
  property int, where it wrapped to -824362432. Nothing was ever refused again
  until a line turned ten seconds old: on the rig on 2026-09-23 one Next
  walked through six stations 1.5 s apart and one PlayPause started and
  stopped the stream three times. The Python test saw only the Python side.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MprisCommandGate.qml

find:
      property double lastSeq: 0

replace:
      property int lastSeq: 0

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_mpriscommandgate.qml::test_a_line_read_twice_is_obeyed_once.
  Line-neutral.
